# Rollbar

> Rollbar is error monitoring for software teams. It alerts you the moment code in production breaks, groups each bug into one item, and shows the line of code, the deploy, and the user session behind every error. Resolve, Rollbar's AI agent, can then write a tested pull request for the errors you choose.

Rollbar is used by more than 64,000 people. It processes more than 2 billion errors a month, alerts in under 3 seconds from the time an error occurs, and is SOC 2 and ISO 27001 certified.

Rollbar has two product lines. Observability is the self-serve product: Error Monitoring, Session Replay, deploy tracking, the Resolve agent, and an MCP server for AI coding agents. Factory (Rollbar Lines) is a service in which a Rollbar team installs an agent on the customer's own cloud account or data center, where it works the team's tickets and returns tested pull requests for people to approve.

## Key facts

- Rollbar does not charge per seat. Every plan, including Free, has unlimited users and unlimited projects.
- The Free plan costs $0 forever and includes 5,000 error occurrences and 1,000 session replays a month, with no credit card required.
- Paid plans are usage-based. Essentials starts at $9 a month for 10,000 occurrences, and Advanced starts at $13 a month for 10,000 occurrences. Enterprise pricing is custom for more than 80 million events a month.
- Annual billing costs the same as 10 months of monthly billing.
- When an account reaches its monthly limit, Rollbar stops processing new events by default, so the bill never goes over the plan price. Accounts on Essentials and above can switch on pay-as-you-go events or set a dollar budget for overages.
- Rollbar offers a 14-day free trial of the full Advanced plan with 200,000 occurrences, 10,000 replays, and 15,000 AI credits.
- Rollbar maintains official SDKs for JavaScript (browser and Node.js), Python, Ruby, PHP, Java and Android, .NET, Go, Apple platforms, and React Native, and community SDKs for other languages and frameworks.
- Alerts go to Slack, Microsoft Teams, email, webhooks, PagerDuty, and other on-call tools. Rollbar can open and close issues in Jira and other trackers automatically.

## Products

- [Error Monitoring](https://rollbar.com/error-monitoring): Groups similar errors by stack trace and message, shows the line of code, the deploy, and the last person to change that code, and routes alerts to the right people.
- [Session Replay](https://rollbar.com/session-replay): Records the clicks, scrolls, inputs, and page changes that led up to a frontend error and attaches the replay to the error itself. Privacy classes mask or exclude sensitive inputs.
- [Resolve](https://rollbar.com/resolve): An AI agent that takes the production errors you assign it, applies a fix in an isolated environment, runs your tests, and only then opens a pull request for you to review. You set which errors it works on, how often, and how much it can spend.
- [MCP server](https://rollbar.com/mcp-server): Rollbar's official, open-source (MIT) MCP server gives AI coding agents such as Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex direct access to errors, stack traces, deploys, and session replays. Source: [github.com/rollbar/rollbar-mcp-server](https://github.com/rollbar/rollbar-mcp-server).
- [Platform overview](https://rollbar.com/platform): How Error Monitoring, Session Replay, deploy tracking, and Resolve fit together.
- [Rollbar Lines (Factory)](https://rollbar.com/factory): A Rollbar team installs an agent on your own systems, writes the operating documents for your repositories, and stays to tune it. A person on your team approves every change.
- [Integrations](https://rollbar.com/integrations): Source control, deploy tools, issue trackers, chat, and on-call tools.

